# AddressSanitizer suppressions (ASAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file>), read by
# the asan-ubsan job of the nightly workflow (m5b-nightly-quality).
#
# Empty on purpose: what the first ASAN + UBSAN runs found was in SIANN code and
# was fixed. A suppression is for a finding in third-party code only, one line
# each (interceptor_via_fun:<function> or interceptor_via_lib:<library>), with a
# comment line directly above it giving the reason: the finding, the upstream
# issue, and why it cannot be fixed here. test/native-quality-options.test.js
# fails on a suppression without one.
